            "cve_id": "CVE-2026-61789",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/bytebase/dbhub/security/advisories/GHSA-j656-3hf2-fvjc",
            "summary": "Read-only mode can be bypassed on the MySQL and MariaDB connectors, allowing arbitrary writes and DDL (for example DROP TABLE) through a query that passes the read-only check. DBHub treats \"--\" as a comment regardless of the next character, but MySQL and MariaDB only start a \"--\" comment when it is followed by whitespace, so a statement hidden after \"--\" is ignored by the read-only check yet executed by the database. The MySQL/MariaDB connectors run with multipleStatements enabled and execute the original query string.",
            "severity": "high",
            "updated_at": "2026-07-10T20:23:36Z",
